sentences.t:
Nondum praecipites cingebant oppida fossae;
non tuba directi, non aeris cornua flexi,
non galeae, non ensis erat:

sentences.l:
Not yet did sheer ditches ring the towns;
there was no trumpet of straight bronze, no horns of bent bronze,
no helmets, no sword:

sentences.t:
fugere pudor verumque fidesque;
In quorum subiere locum fraudesque dolique
insidiaeque et vis et amor sceleratus habendi.

sentences.l:
shame fled, and truth, and good faith;
into whose place came in frauds and tricks
and ambushes and force and the criminal love of having.

sentences.t:
Inminet exitio vir coniugis, illa mariti;
lurida terribiles miscent aconita novercae;
filius ante diem patrios inquirit in annos.

sentences.l:
The husband looms over his wife's destruction, she over her husband's;
frightful stepmothers mix livid aconite;
the son inquires into his father's years before the day.
